    "insert": "The provided exposé discusses the utilization of Large Language Models to create personalized learning paths for students. It aimes to adress learning differences between individual students by developing a teaching agent that can adapt the students needs. It is planned to conduct an iterative study where the agent is tested and afterwards reviewed to enable for continuous optimization of a new specialized model.\n\nYour topic is well chosen and part of active research. It is therefore suitable for the task provided.\n\nOne important aspect of the exposé is to stage the problem of domain, identify a gap in existing research elaborate research question that can be answered in a Bachelor thesis. You should describe your problem and how your work is connected to existing research. The questions should contain the precise aspects of the research and not state the general direction of it. It is a good idea to examine the agents impact on individual students and as you mention establishing specific criteria for designing the personalized learning paths. Stating what exactly you want to examine (e.g. how the model can help a vocabulary) would set a reasonable goal for your research and how you plan to achieve it.\n\nSupporting your claims and utilizing existing research is vital in the scientific context. Your exposé must therefore include correct citations. There are several key aspects in your text that lack a quote. This defects the validity of your entire paper. I have marked them in the editor. Also your bibliography is not attached to your exposé (looks like a LaTeX error). I can therefore not check the validity of your sources. The singel paper included by Colace et al. seems to match your topic well. To strengthen the expressiveness of your research you should included even more matching literature.\n\nAnother important aspect of scientific writing are precise formulations. Doing so indicates the reader that you understand the topic and helps indicate the direction of your research. It is a good idea to examine many different aspects of teaching agent. Yet, your exposé is sometimes formulated to general, leaving a feeling of directionless (I have marked these in the editor). Precisely stating what you plan to do would help to answer the research questions and show up a clear line of thought. \n\nThe assignment states that research planned should lie within the scope of a Bachelor thesis. You plan on conducting a iterative study with at least three repetitions. Therefore there is only very little time for each iteration and therefore threatens the quality of the research. The design of the creation of your model also makes it prone to overfitting as you plan on train and evaluate it on the same group of subject several time. Furthermore, the creation of a new model also exceeds the scope of your research as you state to mainly focus on finding important factors of designing personalized learning paths. By focussing on your initial direction of research you could avoid both problems and take a more in-depth look at what is necessary for creating good individual learning paths."
